          title: "Who knew, and who did not",
          body: "John savours the irony: the **master of the feast** tasted the miracle and had no idea where it came from, while the **servants who had drawn** it *knew*. The sign is disclosed not to the important but to those who did what they were told (v. 5). The perfect participle **γεγενημένον**, “having become,” quietly states the accomplished fact: the water *is now* wine.",
