          refs: ['g2.10.19', 'g2.10.22'],
          lemma: "τὸν καλὸν οἶνον ἕως ἄρτι",
          title: "The best wine kept for last",
          body: "The steward means it as a compliment on catering; John means it as a parable. The world serves its best first and declines into the lesser; in Jesus the order is reversed — **the good wine is kept until now.** The abundance and the timing together announce that the long-awaited new thing has arrived, and it surpasses the old.",
