          lemma: "τὸ πάσχα",
          title: "A Passover — and a cleansing placed early",
          body: "This is the first of **three Passovers** John records (2:13; 6:4; 11:55), the scaffolding on which he hangs a ministry of roughly three years. It also raises a famous question: John sets the temple cleansing at the *start* of Jesus’ public work, while Matthew, Mark, and Luke place it in the final week. Some suppose two cleansings; more likely each Evangelist has arranged it for his own purpose — John using it up front as a programmatic sign of what Jesus has come to do.",
