          id: 'a2.19.1',
          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g2.19.8', 'g2.19.12'],
          lemma: "Λύσατε τὸν ναὸν τοῦτον",
          title: "“Destroy this temple”",
          body: "The word switches from **ἱερόν** (the precinct, vv. 14–15) to **ναός** — the *sanctuary*, the dwelling-place of God — and there lies the riddle. Jesus speaks of his own body as the true meeting-point of God and humanity (v. 21). The **three days** are the resurrection in advance; the imperative “destroy” hands his hearers, unwittingly, the role they will play. It is a saying so charged that it is thrown back at him at his trial (Mark 14:58) and at the cross (Mark 15:29).",
