          refs: ['g2.20.5', 'g2.20.9'],
          lemma: "Τεσσεράκοντα καὶ ἓξ ἔτεσιν",
          title: "“Forty-six years”",
          body: "Herod the Great began rebuilding the temple around 20/19 BC; forty-six years later places this scene near **AD 27–28**, a useful anchor for dating Jesus’ ministry (the work was not fully finished until the AD 60s). The objection is also pure Johannine irony: they measure a *building* while he speaks of his *body* — misunderstanding the sign by taking it literally, as characters in this Gospel so often do.",
