          refs: ['g2.23.14', 'g2.23.22'],
          lemma: "πολλοὶ ἐπίστευσαν … θεωροῦντες",
          title: "A believing that isn’t yet trust",
          body: "Many “believed in his name” — but the next verse says Jesus did *not* entrust himself to them. John draws a careful line between a faith produced merely by **signs** (impressive but shallow) and the faith that receives the person. Signs are meant to lead somewhere; a belief that stops at the wonder has not yet arrived.",
