          body: "A pointed wordplay the English can only footnote: the crowd **ἐπίστευσαν** (“believed”) *in* him (v. 23), but Jesus **οὐκ ἐπίστευεν** (“did not believe / entrust”) *himself* to them — the very same verb, **πιστεύω**, turned back on itself. Their trust in him was not matched by his trust in them, for he saw straight through it.",
