          body: "The chapter ends on Jesus’ unsettling insight into the human heart — the same all-seeing knowledge that named Nathanael under the fig tree (1:47–48) and will lay bare the Samaritan woman’s life (4:18). **ἄνθρωπος** here is *humankind* in general: he needs no witness about people, because he reads them. It is the perfect hinge into the next scene, where “a man” — Nicodemus — comes to him by night (3:1).",
